  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "In avis that can remove their head (by parenting it to an empty and editing the empty or directly by constraining the head) the voice _sometimes_ ends up out of position when the head is returned to the body. It's been described as roughly 180 degrees offset from where the voice should be to a listener (ie the affected avatar's voice comes from behind when they are standing right in front of you, or from the opposite side when they are standing beside you.)\n\nThis can only be solved by avatar switching once it happens. And yes this is a perennial regression that just keeps returning. 💀\n\nThis has been a sometimes issue for at least a week or two of builds.",
